Hi @all,
Maybe this was asked before many times (don't kill me)
is sombody working on a ipsec nat module for iptables, like kernel 2.2.X
has it?
If not, is it planed?
I found nothing about that in pom docs or elseware, related kernel Stuff
2.4.X
I read for one client , it possible to make ipsec run behind a nat wall,
But my tries fail.
Has anybody an example script that makes this work.
After all all other modules h323 , pptp etc works fine for me now
The solution with nat traversal clients don't makes me very happy at the
moment
Cause ssh sentinel for windows , is not free for use.
Regards

